to a SQL type of database.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:34.210
And of course, you're
using Firestore, Firebase,

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:36.890
which shows a lot of
the power that it has,

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:40.070
especially like for
startup innovating quickly.

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:44.620
So what was the
decision criteria like,

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.360
what was the
rationale behind going

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:48.760
with Firebase from the start?

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:50.410
DAN SCHLOSSER: Yeah, absolutely.

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:54.520
The decision to go with
Firestore over a SQL database

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:58.150
was one, to optimize for
speed without sacrificing

00:10:58.150 --> 00:10:59.710
user experience.

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:02.020
I had used the Firebase
Realtime Database

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:03.910
in the past, which
was phenomenal

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:06.760
for getting a project done
in a weekend or something

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:09.760
but what we wanted
was a database that

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:14.980
would serve every request
really quickly while also

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:17.200
letting us move
quickly and adapt

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:19.510
based on the needs of
our customers' changing.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:21.550
In a startup, the only
thing that's constant

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.950
is change, so we
didn't want to be

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:28.480
doing SQL migrations every
week as we added new features.

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:31.210
Firestore has been really
amazing from a performance

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:34.300
perspective and it's
allowed us to do

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:36.580
the kinds of complex
queries that we

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:39.550
need to power our experience.

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:43.450
That decision is holed up
and we may introduce some SQL

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:46.495
databases in the future
but so far, Firestore

00:11:46.495 --> 00:11:48.070
has served us well.

00:11:48.070 --> 00:11:49.570
FILLIPO MADELLA:
Dan, this is great.

